":"flaske","pos":"verb","n_etimologia":2,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"Possibly; or from; obscure","significato":"flaske sig – work out, pan out","termine_origine":"flasken","catena":[{"codice":"nds-de","nome":"German Low German","termine":"flasken","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"nds-de","ambiti":[],"via":"","alternative":[{"codice":"nds-de","nome":"German Low German","termine":"flasken","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"gml","nome":"Middle Low German","termine":"vlaschen","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"gem-pro","nome":"Proto-Germanic","termine":"*flataz","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"gmw-pro","nome":"Proto-West Germanic","termine":"*flint","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"testo":"From German Low German flasken, from Middle Low German vlaschen, of obscure origin: * possibly from a regional verb built from an older root meaning \"flat\" (compare Proto-Germanic *flataz): with a verb-forming suffix -sk- or -k-. According to this view, a prehistoric form *flat-ka could have yielded"}]}